"""Black-box checks for git-wt and its wrappers, driven through their
command names on throwaway repos laid out the way git-wt expects:
<case>/projects/<repo> with a bare <case>/origin.git and worktrees landing
in <case>/worktrees/.

gh, fzf and (where a check needs it) $SHELL are stand-ins. tmux runs on a
scratch TMUX_TMPDIR, so the user's own server is never touched.

The bootstrap copy/link rules themselves live in test-git-wt-bootstrap; only
the rule that a linked path never shows up in git status is checked here.

Run: scripts/tests/test-git-wt                      (or `mise run test`)
     scripts/tests/test-git-wt --only remove        sections whose name matches
     scripts/tests/test-git-wt --via-wrappers       every check through git-wt-<cmd>
     TEST_GIT_WT_KEEP=1 scripts/tests/test-git-wt   keep the scratch dir
"""

